+/*
+ * socrates console 2x (2026-11-06): the panel is 1440x3200 and the stock
+ * 8x16 iso font is unreadable at that pixel density - by eye and by photo
+ * OCR alike, and this board has no debug UART, so the text console is the
+ * only diagnostic channel. Every glyph pixel is rendered as a 2x2 block:
+ * the glyph data stays 8x16 (iso_font, vc_render_char), but the CELL the
+ * console sees is doubled. All cell geometry - rows/columns, the paint
+ * origin, the cursor, scrolling, clears - uses the doubled macros below;
+ * only the 32bpp paint path is scaled (that is the only depth this board
+ * hands the kernel: DarwinBootVideoFromGop rejects every other format).
